#: ../../source/docs/common-compassless.rst:5
#: 89bf78ef24da4496ad7401ec11052b70
msgid "Compass-less Operation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compassless.rst:7
#: fefa2f136d984d0d8369713b0ff5d17b
msgid "Operation without a compass has been possible for Plane for a long time. However, recent additions of alternative yaw sources has opened the possibility of compass-less operation of multicopters, quadplanes and rovers.  The available mechanism are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compassless.rst:9
#: 30f698cc6f5b4fada577d2a1480d3e9e
msgid "Align yaw to GPS after takeoff (Plane only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compassless.rst:10
#: 0ec2d938f36a4e4db794cf81dc1d3e48
msgid "GSF (Gaussian Sum Filter) estimates the heading by comparing a single GPS's outputs to the IMU movements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compassless.rst:11
#: 8787dcf6fa3644ba8575163bf93b280d
msgid ":ref:`GPS-for-Yaw <common-gps-for-yaw>` uses the position of two UBlox F9 GPSs to calculate yaw"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compassless.rst:12
#: 4753cd72d2d5476a97536cd893ddf58c
msgid ":ref:`Intel RealSense T265 <common-vio-tracking-camera>` can provide yaw relative to its startup yaw"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compassless.rst:15
#: f5dbd413a5ef46feb548c9563231253f
msgid "Align Yaw to GPS (Plane only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compassless.rst:17
#: 2bc2251d2edb42e68201cd6685ea84fb
msgid "On Plane, a steady GPS heading is used after takeoff to align the /attitude/velocity/position/heading estimation filters (EKFs) for yaw. This usually occurs a few seconds after takeoff on Planes without compass. However, this approach cannot be used for Quadplane's VTOL navigation, since it needs to be accurate very shortly after takeoffs with no GPS velocity or heading inputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compassless.rst:21
#: 50f871c5c2ac4cd8863f2cfe399444d2
msgid "GSF"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compassless.rst:23
#: 467828c50aea47ce8a37df8d8db60ff3
msgid "ArduPilot supports a Gaussian Sum Filter (GSF) which takes IMU and GPS inputs to compute a probable heading, if a yaw source (like a compass) is unavailable, or unhealthy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compassless.rst:25
#: e46c9a259cd145c997fd0d2ffbb47a0e
msgid "Currently, it does not function well for QuadPlane VTOL tailsitters, since their nose is pointed vertically in VTOL flight. Compasses are still recommended for Tailsitters. Also, for this to work well at all, vibration should be low and the GPS velocity accurate, see below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compassless.rst:27
#: 4ecb0568e5c14f21802f8147fcbaaa2d
msgid "GSF depends on good velocity reports from the GPS. Do not attempt with older generation GPSes, and use at least UBlox M8 or equivalent performance GPSes. Also, be sure GPS view of the sky is unobstructed throughout the flight. Otherwise, poor heading estimation will result. On Plane, if the GPS accuracy is impaired by interference from other nearby vehicle devices (like cameras, etc.), GSF can result in poorer performance than relying solely on Align Yaw to GPS heading, above. In those cases, it may be better to disable GSF use by setting the :ref:`EK3_GSF_USE_MASK<EK3_GSF_USE_MASK>` = 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compassless.rst:30
#: e4bd571d84ef483fbf283297af884bbc
msgid "Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compassless.rst:32
#: 03c1bdf2abaa48f28cf7d8e8f6f4cf90
msgid "Simply, set :ref:`COMPASS_ENABLE<COMPASS_ENABLE>` = 0. Fallback to the GSF will be automatic if normal default values are being used for EKF parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compassless.rst:34
#: e87bc47c049e4684af09aac9f42afc74
msgid "For configure EKF3 to always use GSF set :ref:`EK3_SRC1_YAW <EK3_SRC1_YAW>` = 8 (GSF)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compassless.rst:37
#: e38fe941d631427386b6136140ac4959
msgid "Operation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compassless.rst:39
#: 50aa0c397e684d40956c5fbec0dece11
msgid "Currently, only Plane will arm if the :ref:`ARMING_SKIPCHK<ARMING_SKIPCHK>` for compass isn't skipped, when no compasses are enabled. Copter and QuadPlane will give an pre-arming failure. Three possible methods to arm Copter and QuadPlane are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compassless.rst:41
#: a6f136e9a6304241a0e6e60d829e44ff
msgid "Enable :ref:`ARMING_SKIPCHK<ARMING_SKIPCHK>` for Compass (don't skip any others!)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compassless.rst:42
#: e1e8d12c2edd4b87a73a2a3a7e0f9a02
msgid "Force arming from ground station."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compassless.rst:43
#: 90680e6fb4884bde9ff43196be6ae121
msgid "Before arming, but after GPS lock has been obtained and EKF origin has been set and is \"using GPS\", pick up the vehicle and walk around in a circle a few meters in diameter. This should allow the GSF to acquire yaw alignment and the message \"EKF yaw alignment complete\" would be sent to the ground station."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compassless.rst:45
#: 101471d5ecb145dba396781b4b3a6699
msgid "If either of the first two methods are used, then the first movements of the vehicle in VTOL position controlled modes may be initially in the wrong direction, but should quickly stop once yaw alignment of the GSF has been obtained. Either fly the vehicle a bit in a non-position controller mode (like STABILIZE or QHOVER), or give the vehicle sufficient clearance for the unknown initial movement direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compassless.rst:47
#: 7e2cae08b0c841f1b312bcd683f82cff
msgid "Afterwards, flight and navigation should be acceptable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-compassless.rst:49
#: 2333a379f8634dcc8234cae3be6dee58
msgid "on Plane, without compass, after arming the vehicle will fall back to DCM (\"DCM Active\"  message over MAVLinK) from EKF3 since it has no yaw sensor yet. This will be flagged in MP HUD as \"Unhealthy AHRS\" or on RC telemetry systems (like CRSF) with a \"AHRS Bad\" message. Ignore this, once the plane starts moving EKF3 will obtain yaw information and align, and operation will switch back to it (\"EKF3 active\")."
msgstr ""

